WEBVTT

00:51.009 --> 00:52.427
Let's just forget it happened.

00:53.052 --> 00:54.637
Let's be mature. Let's be cool about it.

00:54.721 --> 00:56.306
I hope we get along.

00:56.806 --> 00:59.434
Let's be mature. Let's be cool about it.

01:00.935 --> 01:02.062
Okay, then.

01:27.837 --> 01:29.339
This is insane.

01:34.636 --> 01:36.095
Aren't you hungry?

01:36.179 --> 01:37.931
Let's grab something to…

01:57.283 --> 01:58.284
Ha-kyung didn't come home?

01:59.494 --> 02:02.956
What did she say on the phone last night?

02:03.039 --> 02:06.960
She told you not to worry because
she'd end it with Ki-jun no matter what.

02:18.888 --> 02:20.348
Hey! You…

02:20.431 --> 02:22.183
Mom worried about you all night.

02:22.267 --> 02:24.352
Why didn't you tell us
you were staying out?

02:25.895 --> 02:27.814
Did you come straight from work?

02:29.190 --> 02:30.108
Yes.

02:30.984 --> 02:33.069
- Did you eat?
- I'm not hungry.

02:39.534 --> 02:40.994
Mom, food isn't the issue.

02:41.077 --> 02:42.662
Can't you tell?

02:43.538 --> 02:45.206
She couldn't do it.

02:46.249 --> 02:48.418
She's smart and sharp about everything,

02:48.501 --> 02:52.589
but she's clueless when it comes
to what really matters for herself.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.175
Wait here.

03:18.948 --> 03:21.034
- She's crying.
- She is?

03:22.577 --> 03:24.078
- Step aside.
- Mom.

03:25.163 --> 03:26.414
Leave her alone.

03:26.497 --> 03:30.877
Of course, she's upset.
Her fiancé stabbed her in the back.

03:30.960 --> 03:32.295
I knew it.

03:32.378 --> 03:35.590
I knew he was up to no good
when she made excuses for him.

03:35.673 --> 03:38.509
Exactly. She must be really embarrassed.

03:38.593 --> 03:41.679
She has no reason to be embarrassed.
It was all his fault!

03:41.763 --> 03:44.641
Mom, just leave her alone.

03:44.724 --> 03:46.100
Let's give her some time

03:46.184 --> 03:48.353
to get her head together, okay?

03:48.436 --> 03:49.729
Goodness.

04:12.627 --> 04:13.711
This is insane.

04:27.350 --> 04:30.228
The yellow dust has receded overnight,

04:30.311 --> 04:32.146
and today's midday weather will be

04:32.230 --> 04:34.565
closer to that of
early summer than spring.

04:34.649 --> 04:37.318
The temperature will rise to 28°C
during the day in Seoul,

04:37.402 --> 04:40.989
about 7 to 8 degrees higher
than yesterday.

04:48.705 --> 04:50.456
The time between seasons is ambiguous.

04:53.751 --> 04:57.088
You aren't sure whether
you should wear thick or thin clothes.

04:58.673 --> 05:00.049
TRY A SUMMER DELICACY!

05:00.133 --> 05:01.676
- Bye.
- Bye.

05:01.759 --> 05:03.553
COLD BUCKWHEAT NOODLES
SPICY BUCKWHEAT NOODLES

05:05.388 --> 05:06.764
You hesitate between eating

05:06.848 --> 05:09.434
- Thank you.
- something hot or something cold.

05:09.517 --> 05:10.810
- Hello.
- Welcome.

05:16.149 --> 05:17.317
Can I have a hot…

05:17.984 --> 05:19.652
No, I'll have an iced Americano, please.

05:19.736 --> 05:20.945
- One?
- Yes.

05:21.571 --> 05:22.530
Thank you.

05:33.333 --> 05:37.003
So, at times, I'm confused
whether this inexplicable feeling…

05:38.254 --> 05:40.965
is sadness about letting go
of the passing season

05:41.049 --> 05:44.969
or excitement for the new season.

05:50.892 --> 05:54.479
What's clear is that summer is coming.

06:25.426 --> 06:31.057
EPISODE 3
IN BETWEEN SEASONS

07:10.471 --> 07:13.641
I'm off to work.
I made breakfast so make sure to eat.

07:36.122 --> 07:37.373
Man.

07:40.585 --> 07:42.545
Are you going to school?

07:44.380 --> 07:45.882
See you later.

07:45.965 --> 07:47.467
Call me when you're done at the academy.

07:47.550 --> 07:49.552
- Okay.
- Bye.

07:52.972 --> 07:55.475
What's wrong with her?
Is she sensitive in the morning?

07:56.058 --> 07:57.435
She's all grown up.

07:57.518 --> 07:59.353
You can't be dressed like that at home.

08:00.396 --> 08:01.439
This…

08:01.522 --> 08:03.774
Why not? I'm her dad.

08:04.650 --> 08:08.779
Yes. You're a dad who hasn't lived
with his daughter for 14 years.

08:17.955 --> 08:19.081
Breakfast is ready.

08:19.165 --> 08:20.416
Have some before you go.

08:20.500 --> 08:21.751
I'm late for work.

08:25.213 --> 08:27.798
Your car isn't outside.
Did you leave it at work?

08:42.396 --> 08:44.732
Oh, right.

08:44.815 --> 08:45.650
Bye.

08:47.401 --> 08:49.195
This is driving me nuts.

08:51.614 --> 08:52.490
Yes.

08:54.450 --> 08:57.286
No. We didn't find
any car keys in the room.

08:57.870 --> 08:58.788
Really?

08:58.871 --> 09:01.165
Could you please check again,
just in case?

09:01.249 --> 09:02.792
Yes. Thank you.

09:10.466 --> 09:11.717
Yes.

09:13.719 --> 09:15.596
The buoy data over the past week.

09:15.680 --> 09:17.598
BUOY: EQUIPMENT USED
TO OBSERVE WEATHER CONDITIONS AT SEA

09:17.682 --> 09:20.309
It's here. Thank you.

09:28.859 --> 09:31.195
- Forecaster Lee, did you catch a cold?
- Yes.

09:31.279 --> 09:33.489
You should have been careful.

09:34.240 --> 09:35.908
Was it cold last night?

09:36.993 --> 09:37.994
No.

09:48.212 --> 09:49.463
It was hot.

09:50.923 --> 09:52.675
Did you sleep out?

09:52.758 --> 09:54.552
You're wearing
the same clothes as yesterday.

09:56.887 --> 09:57.930
Did you sleep out?

10:00.683 --> 10:01.601
That's personal.

10:02.435 --> 10:04.979
What's going on, Forecaster Lee?

10:05.062 --> 10:06.647
You're making me curious.

10:08.691 --> 10:09.942
Actually…

10:10.026 --> 10:12.820
I'm staying at the training center
while I look for a place.

10:13.779 --> 10:16.657
I can only stay there
until the end of the month.

10:16.741 --> 10:18.200
So I'm living out of a suitcase.

10:18.951 --> 10:20.328
I see.

10:20.411 --> 10:23.164
Assistant Director Shin,
don't you have an extra room?

10:23.247 --> 10:25.958
Didn't you buy an apartment last year?

10:27.668 --> 10:28.628
Did you?

10:29.420 --> 10:31.047
It's not mine. The bank owns it.

10:31.631 --> 10:34.675
I won't be a freeloader. I'll pay rent.

10:34.759 --> 10:37.303
Si-woo, I can't live with anyone.

10:38.804 --> 10:41.682
Where is Director Jin? Is she always late?

10:43.893 --> 10:45.353
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:48.939 --> 10:50.149
That's weird.

10:50.232 --> 10:51.859
She's never been late.

11:21.555 --> 11:23.891
Director Jin, where are you?
The meeting is starting soon.

11:24.850 --> 11:26.352
The traffic is terrible.

11:27.937 --> 11:31.232
It'd be great if Senior Forecaster Um
could start the meeting.

11:40.699 --> 11:43.202
Director Jin is going to be late.

11:43.285 --> 11:45.454
She asked if you could start the meeting.

11:48.874 --> 11:50.292
Good morning.

11:50.376 --> 11:52.086
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

12:05.391 --> 12:07.393
KMA BUS STOP

12:25.494 --> 12:27.913
- Why aren't we starting?
- She isn't here yet.

12:27.997 --> 12:29.248
She isn't?

12:32.668 --> 12:35.087
Soo-jin, did you tell him?

13:02.615 --> 13:04.074
Where is Director Jin?

13:04.992 --> 13:06.994
She isn't checking her messages now.

13:09.955 --> 13:12.041
Ask Senior Forecaster Um
to start the meeting.

13:12.124 --> 13:14.335
I already asked him twice.

13:16.212 --> 13:17.630
But he's still as a rock.

13:21.550 --> 13:23.719
Senior Forecaster Um,
please start the meeting.

13:27.723 --> 13:28.891
Senior Forecaster Um.

13:48.369 --> 13:50.287
I'm sorry. I…

13:50.371 --> 13:52.248
I left my car yesterday and…

13:52.331 --> 13:54.375
I understand. Let's start the meeting.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.584
I'm sorry.

14:07.179 --> 14:08.264
I'm sorry.

14:19.692 --> 14:20.859
Won't you start?

14:21.527 --> 14:22.611
I will.

14:27.157 --> 14:29.577
We'll begin the morning meeting of May 10.

14:29.660 --> 14:30.744
Satellite center--

14:40.045 --> 14:40.921
I'm sorry.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.799
What's the current status?

14:43.883 --> 14:47.011
A wind warning is in effect
on the West Sea due to strong lower wind

14:47.094 --> 14:49.555
at the edge of
an anticyclone in the south.

14:51.974 --> 14:53.017
Now…

14:53.726 --> 14:55.060
Thank you.

15:02.693 --> 15:05.863
If you look at the satellite images,
clouds are rotating clockwise

15:05.946 --> 15:08.657
around Gyeongbuk Province.

15:08.741 --> 15:11.452
- In this case, the inland--
- No. Please go over

15:11.535 --> 15:14.538
the high wind warning
that went into effect two days ago first.

15:15.664 --> 15:16.498
Pardon?

15:17.166 --> 15:20.210
It's chaos here
because of the high wind warning.

15:24.089 --> 15:27.384
Please lift the fishing ban.
What are you doing?

15:27.468 --> 15:29.011
In the last election,

15:29.094 --> 15:31.931
didn't you say you'd help fishermen
make a better living?

15:32.014 --> 15:34.058
We have only two weeks to catch crabs.

15:34.141 --> 15:36.268
You've held us back for two days already.

15:36.352 --> 15:38.228
What do you want us to do?

15:38.312 --> 15:40.981
Don't you know anyone at the coast guard?

15:41.065 --> 15:44.109
Can't the governor
do something about this?

15:44.193 --> 15:45.402
Do something!

15:45.486 --> 15:46.320
No.

15:46.403 --> 15:47.529
COAST GUARD
SENIOR SUPERINTENDENT YOO WON-CHEOL

15:47.613 --> 15:49.531
I understand their situation.

15:49.615 --> 15:51.742
But until the KMA
clears the high wind warning,

15:51.825 --> 15:53.285
they can't set sail.

15:54.119 --> 15:57.665
There are currently nine patrol boats
that can be dispatched.

15:57.748 --> 16:01.919
And there are only about 32 rescue guards
and coast guards in total.

16:02.002 --> 16:04.964
If an accident occurs on the swell waves,

16:05.047 --> 16:06.715
we can't do anything about it!

16:08.092 --> 16:10.427
No means no!

16:11.428 --> 16:12.596
GWANGJU REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

16:12.680 --> 16:15.891
Shouldn't you do something about this?

16:15.975 --> 16:17.726
The sea conditions there…

16:24.525 --> 16:28.028
Well, the west coast wave period

16:28.112 --> 16:30.823
has dropped down to 11.4 seconds.

16:30.906 --> 16:33.784
Looking at the
oceanographic factors there…

16:34.410 --> 16:35.369
I mean…

16:35.452 --> 16:37.121
Let's help her.

16:37.705 --> 16:39.206
Send her the summarized data.

16:52.761 --> 16:53.721
I'm sorry.

16:55.973 --> 16:59.810
I'm really sorry.
I haven't analyzed the situation yet.

17:03.147 --> 17:06.650
Senior Forecaster Um,
could you please take over?

17:10.529 --> 17:12.573
The wave height isn't stable yet.

17:12.656 --> 17:16.035
Considering the long wind drift distance,

17:16.702 --> 17:18.912
the wave height
will not subside immediately.

17:19.621 --> 17:20.748
Is that so?

17:21.331 --> 17:23.917
Goodness.

17:25.919 --> 17:29.006
What do you think,
Severe Weather Forecaster Lee?

17:29.089 --> 17:31.675
The wave height remains the same,
but the wave period

17:31.759 --> 17:33.427
dropped from 14.5 to 11.4 seconds.

17:34.053 --> 17:35.304
The wind speed is dropping

17:35.387 --> 17:37.890
and the swell waves
are gradually subsiding.

17:37.973 --> 17:40.350
So your opinion is different
from Senior Forecaster Um's.

17:41.477 --> 17:42.436
Yes.

17:45.189 --> 17:46.648
What?

17:49.735 --> 17:52.946
The Administrator is calling
because of the high wind warning in Taean.

17:56.200 --> 17:58.702
The local governments
are pressuring the Administrator.

17:58.786 --> 18:00.913
- Goodness.
- This is complicated.

18:00.996 --> 18:02.873
Director Jin, what do you think?

18:04.625 --> 18:06.460
They have different opinions.

18:06.543 --> 18:08.587
You need to make a decision.

18:17.387 --> 18:19.598
Hey, Director Jin.

18:19.681 --> 18:21.183
Considering the wave height deviation,

18:21.266 --> 18:23.143
we'll monitor the situation
for another time section.

18:23.227 --> 18:26.772
TIME SECTION: A PERIOD OF 3 HOURS
IN WHICH WEATHER DATA IS UPDATED

18:32.486 --> 18:33.529
Okay.

18:34.613 --> 18:35.906
Got it.

18:35.989 --> 18:38.575
We'll monitor the conditions
until the next update.

18:38.659 --> 18:40.410
- Report that.
- Yes, sir.

18:40.911 --> 18:42.830
The meeting is over.

18:49.878 --> 18:51.004
I'm sorry.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.757
For what?
For being late or for stuttering?

18:53.841 --> 18:56.009
For having to monitor
the conditions some more.

18:57.344 --> 18:59.471
We can do that. What's the problem?

19:00.472 --> 19:03.350
You'll get annoying complaints
from everywhere.

19:04.434 --> 19:05.435
Director Jin.

19:06.019 --> 19:07.604
I'll take care of that.

19:07.688 --> 19:11.316
As a director, you only need
to look after your team.

19:13.068 --> 19:15.112
Okay. I'm sorry.

19:16.155 --> 19:18.031
It's okay.

19:18.699 --> 19:19.867
Good work.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.451
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

19:30.294 --> 19:33.589
I clearly told him
that you asked him to run the meeting.

19:33.672 --> 19:34.965
Twice.

19:40.804 --> 19:42.681
- Let's get some coffee.
- All right.

19:53.066 --> 19:54.151
Are you okay?

19:54.234 --> 19:58.238
With what? With being late,
stuttering, or being embarrassed?

19:58.322 --> 19:59.615
I'm talking about the cold.

19:59.698 --> 20:01.366
You sneezed really loudly.

20:03.035 --> 20:05.579
I have rhinitis.
It's because the season is changing.

20:38.320 --> 20:39.655
I'll buy it.

20:39.738 --> 20:44.117
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET
SELLING AN AIR PURIFIER

20:44.201 --> 20:45.410
For 300,000 won.

21:07.849 --> 21:09.685
What? Why are you still here?

21:14.856 --> 21:16.191
Didn't you know?

21:16.275 --> 21:18.694
I've been officially transferred here.

21:19.987 --> 21:21.405
Why here of all places?

21:21.488 --> 21:24.116
Ask HR if you're curious.

21:24.199 --> 21:25.701
It was their decision.

21:26.910 --> 21:29.162
So you'll stay here
and keep bumping into me?

21:29.246 --> 21:30.163
Yes.

21:30.247 --> 21:33.375
Working at Headquarters was my dream,
so I'll work hard.

21:33.458 --> 21:36.086
I lost you
because I was chasing that dream.

21:36.169 --> 21:37.337
Am I wrong?

21:38.213 --> 21:41.300
Do you think that was
the only reason for our breakup?

21:41.883 --> 21:42.843
What else was there?

21:42.926 --> 21:45.637
Do you really not know
or are you just pretending?

21:52.477 --> 21:53.729
It doesn't matter anyway.

21:54.313 --> 21:57.149
Because we have nothing
to do with each other now.

22:00.986 --> 22:02.154
Reporter Chae!

22:03.447 --> 22:05.198
Good day, Reporter Chae.

22:12.080 --> 22:14.583
- Who was that?
- A Severe Weather Forecaster.

22:14.666 --> 22:16.835
He was transferred here recently.

22:16.918 --> 22:18.086
How do you know him?

22:19.046 --> 22:21.548
I just know him from work.

22:21.631 --> 22:23.675
I see.

22:27.763 --> 22:30.098
COAST GUARD TELLS FISHERMEN
TO STAY ALERT FOR POSSIBLE ACCIDENTS

22:30.182 --> 22:31.683
STRONG WINDS EXPECTED ON THE WEST COAST

22:31.767 --> 22:32.809
REGULAR FERRY OPERATIONS SUSPENDED

22:32.893 --> 22:34.061
EXTRA CAUTION REQUIRED
FOR MARITIME ACCIDENTS

22:34.144 --> 22:36.855
The warning hasn't been lifted yet.

22:36.938 --> 22:38.356
- Yes.
- That's right.

22:38.440 --> 22:39.775
- Of course.
- We're monitoring the conditions.

22:39.858 --> 22:43.445
I understand this is a problem for you,
but the wave heights are still unstable.

22:43.528 --> 22:45.489
We have to wait a little longer.

22:45.572 --> 22:47.407
Yes. The waves are too high.

22:47.491 --> 22:49.242
- It's too…
- Yes, I understand.

22:49.326 --> 22:50.660
We'd really love

22:50.744 --> 22:52.454
- to lift the warning.
- I see.

22:52.537 --> 22:54.247
- But we can't do that
- Yes, I like crabs.

22:54.331 --> 22:56.291
- as we please.
- It's not on purpose.

22:56.374 --> 22:58.168
- The administration says the waves…
- Yes.

22:58.251 --> 22:59.503
Yes, of course.

22:59.586 --> 23:01.546
- No, it's not like that.
- The message board?

23:01.630 --> 23:02.547
Yes.

23:03.173 --> 23:04.591
Okay.

23:04.674 --> 23:07.677
- Yes. Please hold.
- Yes.

23:07.761 --> 23:08.929
The message board is going crazy.

23:12.432 --> 23:15.769
We're the ones suffering
because the KMA is making a big fuss.

23:15.852 --> 23:18.939
The KMA is killing us, not the sea!

23:19.940 --> 23:21.525
Damn it.

23:21.608 --> 23:24.569
Look at that. There's no high wind.

23:24.653 --> 23:26.404
They know nothing about the sea.

23:26.905 --> 23:29.366
I'll let you know
as soon as I hear from them.

23:30.158 --> 23:31.326
- Yes, okay.
- Yes.

23:31.409 --> 23:33.495
We'll do our best.

23:37.249 --> 23:38.375
Goodness.

23:39.334 --> 23:40.752
I can't handle this.

23:41.503 --> 23:42.921
- Deputy Director Han.
- Yes, sir.

23:43.004 --> 23:44.881
Go to the Chief Team

23:44.965 --> 23:47.092
and get a preliminary report.

23:47.175 --> 23:48.468
"A preliminary report"?

23:49.094 --> 23:51.471
We need one that indicates

23:51.555 --> 23:53.306
when the warning will be lifted.

23:53.390 --> 23:55.976
Otherwise, we'll end up
answering phone calls all day.

23:56.059 --> 23:57.477
Okay.

23:57.561 --> 24:00.438
Assistant Director Kim,
which team is in charge today?

24:01.606 --> 24:02.816
It's Chief Team Two.

24:06.319 --> 24:08.280
Of all teams…

24:08.363 --> 24:10.699
Are you not uncomfortable
seeing me like this?

24:10.782 --> 24:12.534
Oh, are you?

24:12.617 --> 24:14.411
Then you should leave instead.

24:14.494 --> 24:17.038
Be my guest and go to Geneva, you asshole.

24:24.045 --> 24:25.255
What is it?

24:26.006 --> 24:29.092
The high wind warning has been
in effect on the Central West Sea

24:29.176 --> 24:32.012
- for two days already.
- And?

24:32.095 --> 24:35.640
Can you give us a preliminary report
on when it'll be lifted--

24:35.724 --> 24:37.976
Didn't you receive the minutes?

24:38.059 --> 24:39.811
The high wind warning can't be lifted

24:39.895 --> 24:43.773
under the current circumstances
due to dangers posed by swell waves.

24:43.857 --> 24:46.568
So why don't we release
a preliminary report?

24:47.152 --> 24:50.030
Either this afternoon
or early tomorrow morning--

24:50.113 --> 24:52.240
The wave heights are unstable.

24:52.324 --> 24:55.619
I can't release uncertain information
just because we're pressured.

24:55.702 --> 24:56.953
Please wait.

25:02.292 --> 25:03.585
I know you can do it.

25:08.423 --> 25:09.382
What do you mean?

25:10.383 --> 25:11.384
A preliminary report.

25:11.468 --> 25:13.803
You're withholding it on purpose

25:13.887 --> 25:15.889
because of your personal feelings.

25:17.766 --> 25:21.478
Are you saying that
I'm making the crab fishermen suffer

25:21.561 --> 25:24.231
because I want to screw you over?

25:24.314 --> 25:26.441
- Aren't you?
- Mr. Han Ki-jun!

25:27.025 --> 25:28.360
You can talk to me.

25:30.862 --> 25:32.447
I'm the Severe Weather Forecaster,

25:32.530 --> 25:33.823
so talk to me.

25:35.742 --> 25:37.994
Do you know what's going on
in the Office of Spokesperson?

25:38.078 --> 25:39.204
It's impossible to work

25:39.287 --> 25:42.374
because of the complaint calls
from local governments and ministries.

25:42.457 --> 25:44.209
Our work is at a standstill.

25:44.793 --> 25:47.504
Shouldn't the Office of Spokesperson
do at least that much?

25:48.171 --> 25:49.256
What?

25:49.923 --> 25:51.675
- "At least that much"?
- Can't you see

25:51.758 --> 25:54.636
that everyone here is skipping lunch

25:54.719 --> 25:56.930
to analyze data for the high winds?

25:57.013 --> 26:00.308
We're working our asses off
drawing up various scenarios.

26:00.392 --> 26:03.186
You should at least take care
of the complaint calls for us.

26:03.270 --> 26:05.313
Everyone is working
their fingers to the bone.

26:05.397 --> 26:06.940
It's not just you.

26:07.023 --> 26:08.984
You shouldn't be complaining.

26:10.694 --> 26:13.655
It's not your place to interfere.
Stay out of this.

26:14.656 --> 26:16.199
I'm the Severe Weather Forecaster.

26:16.283 --> 26:19.744
In any case,
I'm going to talk to your director.

26:20.495 --> 26:22.205
That's enough, Mr. Lee.

26:23.999 --> 26:25.917
Please return to your office, Mr. Han.

26:26.501 --> 26:27.335
What?

26:28.461 --> 26:29.754
Well…

26:30.922 --> 26:33.049
You want me to leave, just like that?

26:33.133 --> 26:34.801
When there's severe weather,

26:35.885 --> 26:39.097
an accident leads straight to casualties.
Don't you know that?

26:39.597 --> 26:42.809
It's not a matter of screwing anyone over.

26:43.476 --> 26:46.479
So go back to your office
and wait for the notice.

26:55.405 --> 26:58.742
- Well, in any case--
- I said go back and wait.

27:29.481 --> 27:30.774
She'll be okay, right?

27:31.358 --> 27:32.233
What?

27:32.984 --> 27:34.486
I'm talking about Ha-kyung.

27:34.569 --> 27:37.822
She looked so dazed.

27:38.490 --> 27:39.657
I know.

27:39.741 --> 27:42.327
Going to work every day
must be hell for her.

27:43.286 --> 27:47.582
As if having to face Ki-jun
every day at work wasn't enough,

27:47.665 --> 27:50.668
everyone who works with her
knows what happened too.

27:50.752 --> 27:53.838
Still, she has to pretend
to be okay and keep working.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.465
Would you be okay if you were her?

27:58.301 --> 27:59.928
What is it? What are you doing?

28:04.224 --> 28:05.392
Ha-kyung.

28:05.475 --> 28:07.602
If you're having
a hard time at work, quit--

28:07.685 --> 28:08.853
I'm busy.

28:08.937 --> 28:10.688
Oh, okay.

28:14.234 --> 28:15.193
Mom.

28:15.276 --> 28:18.279
Doing nothing is the best way to help her.

28:18.363 --> 28:21.741
She didn't sound good. Is she unwell?

28:38.091 --> 28:38.925
Here.

28:39.551 --> 28:40.760
I said I have rhinitis.

28:42.053 --> 28:43.430
You're quite insensitive.

28:49.352 --> 28:50.645
You have a fever.

28:55.984 --> 28:57.110
Take one now.

29:02.741 --> 29:03.867
What are you doing?

29:03.950 --> 29:05.618
It's just part of the job.

29:05.702 --> 29:07.537
Getting on the good side of my director.

29:16.629 --> 29:20.258
Don't worry. I won't ask you out
just because we slept together once.

29:23.303 --> 29:24.554
Take it now, okay?

29:42.489 --> 29:43.656
Goodness.

29:44.657 --> 29:46.284
- Gosh.
- What?

29:47.786 --> 29:49.245
Wait.

29:49.829 --> 29:51.790
Yes. What?

29:53.208 --> 29:55.251
The sea is calm.

29:56.252 --> 29:58.755
It's calm enough for us to swim in.

29:59.839 --> 30:00.924
What?

30:01.424 --> 30:04.594
We know the sea
like the back of our hands.

30:04.677 --> 30:06.221
What about the sea far away?

30:06.846 --> 30:09.265
Yes. What does it look like now?

30:10.391 --> 30:11.559
Okay.

30:12.060 --> 30:13.603
Could you please tell me

30:13.686 --> 30:16.105
the shape of the clouds
and the direction of the wind?

30:17.065 --> 30:18.358
Okay.

30:22.654 --> 30:24.280
I checked the site.

30:24.364 --> 30:27.075
There are swell waves by the seaside,
and none out at sea.

30:27.158 --> 30:28.368
How did you check it?

30:28.451 --> 30:30.912
Through a captain of a weather ship

30:30.995 --> 30:33.706
who knows the seas at Taean
like the back of his hand.

30:34.290 --> 30:37.126
There's an average
of 18 accidents and 32 casualties

30:37.210 --> 30:39.587
due to swell waves every year.

30:39.671 --> 30:43.424
Most of them knew the sea
like the back of their hands.

30:43.508 --> 30:45.385
The ocean wind is becoming weaker.

30:45.468 --> 30:48.763
The significant wave height is quite tall,

30:48.847 --> 30:51.474
but, as he said,
the wind is getting weaker.

30:52.642 --> 30:53.685
- That's true.
- So if we

30:53.768 --> 30:55.562
bring the warning down to a watch,

30:55.645 --> 30:57.146
big vessels can set sail.

30:57.230 --> 30:59.148
We'll be less pressured,

30:59.232 --> 31:00.859
and the fishermen will be relieved.

31:01.442 --> 31:02.694
If the big vessels depart,

31:02.777 --> 31:04.696
the small ones will follow.

31:04.779 --> 31:05.947
Will you be able to stop them?

31:06.030 --> 31:08.783
Coast Guard is worried about
not being able to control them.

31:09.367 --> 31:11.119
Do you want to keep the warning then?

31:16.124 --> 31:17.792
What do you think?

31:19.544 --> 31:21.462
When it's hard to make a decision,

31:22.505 --> 31:24.215
go with the figures.

31:26.634 --> 31:28.136
But it's crab fishing season.

31:28.219 --> 31:30.388
I can't ignore the fishermen.

31:31.222 --> 31:34.475
Or trust Forecaster Lee's hunch

31:34.559 --> 31:36.728
and bring the warning down to a watch.

31:37.812 --> 31:41.649
Who knows?
Maybe Poseidon will calm the waves.

31:45.236 --> 31:47.155
You talk as if it's none of your business.

31:49.532 --> 31:52.368
The director is responsible
for making a decision,

31:52.452 --> 31:53.661
not me.

31:54.287 --> 31:55.705
Right.

32:21.981 --> 32:23.399
This is Han Ki-jun
of the Office of Spokesperson.

32:23.483 --> 32:27.403
Here's the conclusion
our team has reached as of 3:23 p.m.

32:27.487 --> 32:28.488
Sir.

32:28.571 --> 32:30.782
- It's the Chief Team.
- Will they lift it?

32:30.865 --> 32:32.408
Let me hear it.

32:32.492 --> 32:33.576
Please go ahead.

32:33.660 --> 32:36.788
Strong winds and waves on the west coast
have eased to a watch level,

32:36.871 --> 32:40.083
but given the large variation
in significant wave height in the region,

32:40.166 --> 32:41.876
we'll watch the situation until 9 p.m.,

32:41.960 --> 32:45.046
and decide whether
to lower it or lift it completely.

32:45.546 --> 32:47.632
Wait, Director Jin. What did you say?

32:49.509 --> 32:52.095
Director Jin. Well… Director Jin!

33:00.520 --> 33:01.562
Goodness.

33:01.646 --> 33:03.398
- Here we go again.
- This is the Office of Spokesperson.

33:04.107 --> 33:06.234
- Yes.
- This is the Office of Spokesperson.

33:06.317 --> 33:08.277
- This is the Office of Spokesperson.
- Yes.

33:08.361 --> 33:10.655
- It'll last a little longer.
- The warning?

33:10.738 --> 33:11.948
- I'm sorry.
- No.

33:12.031 --> 33:14.033
I'll send the notice then.

33:14.117 --> 33:15.201
Okay.

33:17.453 --> 33:19.747
Your forecast is more conservative
than I thought.

33:20.832 --> 33:23.209
I made a decision
based on figures and data.

33:23.292 --> 33:26.754
There's one more thing that clearly exists
between the figures and the data.

33:27.547 --> 33:28.673
It's called a hunch.

33:28.756 --> 33:30.717
And mine has almost never been wrong.

33:33.594 --> 33:35.179
- Forecaster Lee.
- Yes?

33:37.098 --> 33:40.226
Forecasting is a science.
If you want to remain on my team,

33:40.309 --> 33:43.646
base your statements only
on scientific evidence, not on your hunch.

33:43.730 --> 33:44.981
Got it?

33:51.320 --> 33:54.073
I'll send out a notice
saying that the high wind warning

33:54.157 --> 33:56.993
on the west coast will be maintained
from 4 p.m. to 9 p.m.

34:02.040 --> 34:03.583
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:03.666 --> 34:04.959
SEND NOTICE?
YES

34:05.043 --> 34:05.918
THE NOTICE HAS BEEN SENT

34:06.002 --> 34:08.171
WEST SEA COAST GUARD STATION

34:12.925 --> 34:16.387
NOTICE
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:18.431 --> 34:20.141
APPLICABLE AREA
CENTRAL WEST SEA, EAST SEA

34:27.648 --> 34:28.816
Really?

34:30.777 --> 34:32.028
Okay.

34:32.945 --> 34:33.863
Yes.

34:34.614 --> 34:35.740
Okay!

34:36.866 --> 34:40.119
Goodness, the weather is killing me now.

34:41.329 --> 34:42.747
Let's go home.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.875
- We can't go out today.
- Again?

34:45.958 --> 34:48.169
- Darn it.
- Seriously?

34:48.252 --> 34:50.213
- Come here.
- Goodness.

34:50.296 --> 34:51.839
- Have a drink.
- I can't believe it.

35:02.141 --> 35:04.227
Who's going to eat all this?

35:04.977 --> 35:07.772
I won't ask you to eat it,
so stop nagging.

35:07.855 --> 35:09.982
Go to the seafood section

35:10.066 --> 35:12.360
and ask them when they're getting loaches.

35:12.443 --> 35:14.028
Why? Will you make loach soup?

35:14.529 --> 35:16.114
Ha-kyung doesn't like that.

35:16.197 --> 35:18.825
- Why are you cooking it again?
- Shall I go?

35:18.908 --> 35:20.284
No, I'll go.

35:22.829 --> 35:25.414
Who makes loach soup at home these days?

35:25.498 --> 35:27.875
You can just order it online
and have it delivered.

35:27.959 --> 35:29.836
She's something else.

35:37.426 --> 35:39.262
Look who's here.

35:39.846 --> 35:40.847
Hi, Soo-ja.

35:41.597 --> 35:42.515
Mrs. Lee?

35:43.099 --> 35:45.143
Long time no see.

35:45.726 --> 35:48.062
Have you been ill or something?

35:48.146 --> 35:50.523
I haven't seen you at the gym in ages.

35:50.606 --> 35:54.026
My youngest had a baby recently.

35:54.110 --> 35:55.820
She needed postpartum care,

35:55.903 --> 35:57.989
so I was in America for a few months.

35:58.072 --> 36:00.616
I see. Did she have a son or a daughter?

36:00.700 --> 36:01.868
A daughter.

36:01.951 --> 36:03.244
That's great.

36:03.327 --> 36:05.621
Daughters are the best.

36:05.705 --> 36:07.582
Your younger daughter got married, right?

36:08.416 --> 36:09.709
I felt really bad

36:09.792 --> 36:11.961
because I couldn't attend the wedding.

36:12.044 --> 36:13.004
Wait a minute.

36:13.087 --> 36:15.548
Let me give you some congratulatory money.

36:15.631 --> 36:17.758
No, you don't have to do that.

36:17.842 --> 36:20.011
Yes, I do.

36:20.094 --> 36:21.929
You gave so much to my daughter.

36:22.013 --> 36:24.557
No, it's okay.

36:27.768 --> 36:30.354
She didn't get married.

36:30.438 --> 36:31.355
What?

36:31.939 --> 36:34.650
- The wedding was called off.
- Why?

36:34.734 --> 36:37.612
You bragged that
he was a government employee

36:37.695 --> 36:40.573
working with your daughter
in the same company.

36:40.656 --> 36:43.492
Did you brag about that jerk, Han Ki-jun?

36:43.576 --> 36:45.703
- Be quiet.
- What happened?

36:45.786 --> 36:47.496
Was there a problem?

36:47.580 --> 36:49.415
No, not really.

36:49.498 --> 36:52.668
You know how even married couples
split up all the time.

36:53.252 --> 36:55.421
I thought he was awful,

36:55.504 --> 36:57.757
so I called it off.

36:57.840 --> 36:59.383
I see.

36:59.467 --> 37:02.178
You must be really upset.

37:02.970 --> 37:04.764
Your older daughter was divorced.

37:04.847 --> 37:07.767
Now your younger daughter's wedding
got called off.

37:08.392 --> 37:10.186
I was the one who called it off.

37:10.269 --> 37:13.522
I'm glad you're okay
after going through that.

37:14.273 --> 37:16.108
I would have been sick in bed.

37:16.192 --> 37:18.569
Why would anyone
be sick in bed because of that?

37:18.653 --> 37:22.657
You should pay attention
when someone's talking.

37:22.740 --> 37:26.410
My daughters weren't dumped.
They dumped them.

37:26.494 --> 37:27.912
Hey, tell her.

37:27.995 --> 37:30.456
Did you divorce him or did he divorce you?

37:30.539 --> 37:31.624
Let's go, Mom.

37:31.707 --> 37:32.750
- Wait.
- Bye.

37:32.833 --> 37:34.335
- Bye.
- Why don't you understand?

37:34.418 --> 37:36.587
- Don't you have any ears?
- Mom, let's go.

37:36.671 --> 37:37.922
They have good loaches.

37:38.005 --> 37:39.090
- Do they?
- Yes.

37:39.173 --> 37:41.300
- That old witch.
- Let's go.

37:50.393 --> 37:51.727
- Good work.
- Good work.

37:52.228 --> 37:54.397
A new seafood noodles restaurant opened.

37:54.480 --> 37:56.065
That sounds good.

37:56.732 --> 37:58.276
Won't you join us?

37:58.359 --> 38:00.152
No. You guys enjoy it.

38:00.236 --> 38:02.029
See you tomorrow.

38:02.113 --> 38:03.030
- Okay.
- Let's go.

38:03.114 --> 38:04.031
- Is it good?
- Yes.

38:06.826 --> 38:08.119
Aren't you going home?

38:08.202 --> 38:11.706
I am. Darn, my back hurts.

38:15.918 --> 38:16.961
Oh…

38:17.503 --> 38:19.797
- See you tomorrow then.
- See you.

38:24.093 --> 38:25.970
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes?

38:27.138 --> 38:28.973
Don't you have anything to say to me?

38:29.056 --> 38:30.266
No, not really.

38:33.686 --> 38:36.314
What is it? Do you have something to say?

38:39.900 --> 38:41.944
You might not like me,

38:42.028 --> 38:44.363
but work is work.

38:45.114 --> 38:46.115
Right.

38:46.741 --> 38:49.201
Being late for the meeting was my fault.

38:49.285 --> 38:52.496
But I thought you could cover for me.

38:52.580 --> 38:53.706
I see.

38:55.333 --> 38:57.335
Then you should have given a proper order.

39:00.004 --> 39:02.923
Well, it'd be uncomfortable

39:03.007 --> 39:06.010
to have someone much older than you
as a subordinate.

39:06.552 --> 39:07.595
It could be awkward.

39:07.678 --> 39:11.057
But when we work, you're my superior.

39:11.140 --> 39:13.392
And I'm someone who follows your orders.

39:15.227 --> 39:17.438
So you should have given me
a proper order.

39:19.774 --> 39:21.817
That's what your position entails.

39:21.901 --> 39:23.527
If you delay making a decision,

39:23.611 --> 39:26.238
people will complain more like earlier.

39:26.322 --> 39:27.406
If it's ambiguous,

39:27.490 --> 39:30.242
people will voice their opinions
and insist they're right.

39:30.326 --> 39:32.036
If you don't give a proper order,

39:32.119 --> 39:33.579
nobody will follow your lead.

39:35.456 --> 39:36.832
Do you understand?

39:37.416 --> 39:38.751
Yes, I do.

39:40.127 --> 39:42.546
Even if you do,
you'll struggle for a while.

39:43.255 --> 39:44.340
From now on,

39:44.965 --> 39:46.425
I won't be late.

39:47.385 --> 39:49.970
Still, if anything like that

39:50.054 --> 39:52.264
happens again by any chance,

39:52.348 --> 39:55.768
please take over my place.

39:58.396 --> 39:59.730
It's an order.

40:02.650 --> 40:04.735
Okay. See you tomorrow.

40:05.653 --> 40:06.779
Bye.

40:30.594 --> 40:31.554
Yes?

40:31.637 --> 40:33.806
Ha-kyung. You should come home late.

40:34.849 --> 40:35.683
Why?

40:36.350 --> 40:39.019
Mom is drinking soju straight up.

40:46.986 --> 40:53.117
The one I loved so much

40:54.785 --> 41:00.082
- I lost him
- Okay.

41:14.555 --> 41:18.184
I'll come to your place
to pick up the air purifier.

41:18.267 --> 41:20.269
So can you give me a 20,000 won discount?

41:20.352 --> 41:23.314
Can you come to this address
to pick it up tonight?

41:23.397 --> 41:24.440
Yes.

41:25.941 --> 41:29.236
APARTMENT 1201, BUILDING 308,
7, SHINJEONG-RO, DONGJAK-GU

41:50.633 --> 41:51.467
What the…

41:56.764 --> 41:57.806
Darn it.

41:57.890 --> 41:59.183
PLEASE KNOCK

42:04.688 --> 42:06.482
Do you live here alone?

42:06.565 --> 42:07.650
What?

42:07.733 --> 42:09.693
Why don't you lock the bathroom door?

42:11.237 --> 42:12.530
I'm not used to doing that.

42:13.614 --> 42:14.740
Come on.

42:26.544 --> 42:28.963
- Are you a guest?
- What?

42:29.046 --> 42:30.589
Why are you standing there?

42:46.272 --> 42:48.148
- Eat some fruit.
- Okay.

42:53.237 --> 42:55.614
Were you taken aback earlier?

42:57.241 --> 42:58.826
Your dad is so silly, isn't he?

42:59.994 --> 43:00.911
Is he in his room?

43:03.747 --> 43:06.000
Don't be like that to him.

43:07.084 --> 43:10.713
He doesn't know anything
because he hasn't been living with us.

43:10.796 --> 43:12.172
Please be nice to--

43:12.256 --> 43:14.675
- I feel the same.
- What?

43:16.760 --> 43:18.721
I don't know anything…

43:21.348 --> 43:23.392
because I've never lived with Dad.

44:11.440 --> 44:12.775
Seriously?

44:30.250 --> 44:33.295
I'M OFF TO WORK.
I MADE BREAKFAST SO MAKE SURE TO EAT!

44:46.350 --> 44:47.726
By the way,

44:47.810 --> 44:50.813
Deputy Director Han's ex-fiancée…

44:51.355 --> 44:52.398
Yes?

44:52.481 --> 44:54.983
I heard they had a big fight
in front of the Office of Spokesperson.

44:55.067 --> 44:58.362
She even slapped him in front of everyone.

45:01.240 --> 45:04.159
She said she'd never give up
the apartment.

45:34.314 --> 45:35.649
You're home already?

45:35.732 --> 45:37.734
I'm sorry the house was a mess.

45:37.818 --> 45:40.404
I was busy getting ready for work.

45:41.530 --> 45:45.117
- Cleaning up must've been a lot of work.
- Yu-jin.

45:47.119 --> 45:50.831
I asked you to at least
put away the dishes after you ate.

45:50.914 --> 45:52.583
I was too busy, so I forgot.

45:52.666 --> 45:54.585
I told you they attracted fruit flies.

45:55.294 --> 45:58.630
That's because you put
a banana peel in the trash can.

45:58.714 --> 46:01.091
- I did that only once.
- You did it more than once.

46:01.175 --> 46:02.134
I…

46:04.511 --> 46:06.221
Never mind. Forget it.

46:06.305 --> 46:10.142
Fine. You cleaned the house,
so I'll take the trash out.

46:19.735 --> 46:21.069
Oh, no.

46:21.153 --> 46:23.530
Why can't you do anything right?

46:25.574 --> 46:27.993
What about you? Can you do anything right?

46:28.076 --> 46:30.370
What about me? What didn't I do right?

46:33.916 --> 46:36.460
Did you take care of the apartment?

46:37.169 --> 46:38.754
You didn't, did you?

46:40.339 --> 46:41.590
How did you know?

46:41.673 --> 46:43.675
Everyone at the KMA knows except me.

46:44.343 --> 46:47.304
The rent is really expensive here
because it's a short-term lease.

46:47.387 --> 46:49.932
We were going to move
when you got the deposit back.

46:50.015 --> 46:53.560
I need to know what's going on
so we can plan the next move.

46:54.603 --> 46:55.896
Don't think about that.

46:55.979 --> 46:58.482
Why not? Did she say she won't give it up?

46:59.858 --> 47:02.236
How can she be so brazen?

47:02.319 --> 47:05.822
You said half of it was yours.
Why can't you speak up to her?

47:08.283 --> 47:11.161
Out of the 20 million-won savings,
you deposited 5 million.

47:11.245 --> 47:12.788
I paid the rest.

47:12.871 --> 47:16.542
And I paid the deposit,
intermediate payment, and the loan.

47:17.251 --> 47:19.670
Then what does that mean?

47:19.753 --> 47:22.464
Let's halve it? Don't be ridiculous.

47:22.548 --> 47:24.508
You can't get any more brazen than that.

47:26.510 --> 47:27.719
Anyway…

47:27.803 --> 47:30.889
fighting with her at work
won't do us any good.

47:31.431 --> 47:33.308
It's done, so drop it.

47:49.741 --> 47:50.701
Yu-jin.

47:52.995 --> 47:54.913
I said you don't have to do this.

47:54.997 --> 47:57.666
- I can just throw it away on my way out.
- Just go.

47:57.749 --> 47:59.960
I don't want you to hold anything dirty.

48:01.420 --> 48:02.546
You're so sweet.

48:38.707 --> 48:40.792
I used to love sitting here.

48:55.349 --> 48:57.225
Why are you here?

49:02.356 --> 49:03.357
This is the right place.

49:04.983 --> 49:07.319
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET

49:07.402 --> 49:08.945
Are you "issue"?

49:09.571 --> 49:11.156
Are you "jjin"?

49:31.218 --> 49:32.052
Stop looking around.

49:34.304 --> 49:35.472
Okay.

49:40.060 --> 49:41.061
Is this it?

49:41.770 --> 49:42.813
Just go.

49:43.438 --> 49:45.565
I won't sell it to you.
You know why, right?

49:47.359 --> 49:48.443
Yes.

49:52.447 --> 49:54.700
- Are you throwing this out?
- I said just go.

49:58.620 --> 49:59.579
Okay.

50:07.087 --> 50:09.339
- By the way, Director Jin.
- What? What is it?

50:09.423 --> 50:11.466
You've never sold anything online,
have you?

50:12.050 --> 50:13.009
No.

50:13.093 --> 50:15.262
Well, this air purifier.

50:15.345 --> 50:17.597
You said you used it only once to test it.

50:17.681 --> 50:19.474
Then it's like a brand new product.

50:19.558 --> 50:23.061
You can get at least 400,000 won
because it's the bestselling air purifier.

50:23.145 --> 50:25.230
Why would you sell it
for just 300,000 won?

50:27.858 --> 50:29.776
And this is a limited edition speaker.

50:29.860 --> 50:31.695
It's even hard to buy this overseas.

50:31.778 --> 50:33.238
- Really?
- Yes.

50:33.321 --> 50:36.408
If you sell it to an avid fan,
you can get extra money.

50:36.491 --> 50:39.828
Selling a high-end speaker like this
in a full box for half-price

50:39.911 --> 50:41.455
is like giving it away.

50:42.456 --> 50:43.290
What's a full box?

50:43.373 --> 50:45.375
It means the product
is in the original packaging.

50:48.336 --> 50:50.505
Also, here.

50:50.589 --> 50:53.049
The pictures you uploaded.

50:53.717 --> 50:55.927
There are quite a lot of online scams.

50:56.011 --> 50:56.928
Here.

50:57.012 --> 50:59.639
You have to take a picture of your item

50:59.723 --> 51:01.349
with your nickname and date.

51:01.433 --> 51:02.684
It makes you look reliable.

51:03.268 --> 51:04.603
- I see.
- Like this.

51:05.270 --> 51:06.772
Like this.

51:06.855 --> 51:08.940
Upload the pictures.

51:09.024 --> 51:10.442
- Nickname. Yes.
- Upload everything?

51:11.026 --> 51:13.111
Set the date and write "no negotiation."

51:13.195 --> 51:15.739
- That means it's a special price.
- I see.

51:16.281 --> 51:17.491
- And full box.
- Okay.

51:18.158 --> 51:19.367
Overseas limited edition.

51:19.993 --> 51:22.579
- And delivery included.
- Delivery…

51:32.547 --> 51:35.634
I won't ask you out
just because we slept together once.

51:36.718 --> 51:37.803
Why not?

51:39.513 --> 51:41.348
- Pardon?
- What?

51:42.808 --> 51:45.435
What? Why?

51:45.519 --> 51:47.646
You just asked me why not?

51:47.729 --> 51:50.023
No, I didn't say anything.

51:53.109 --> 51:55.570
- Did I do something wrong?
- No.

51:56.238 --> 51:57.739
Did I say something?

51:58.865 --> 52:00.659
Why are you so nervous?

52:01.993 --> 52:03.703
I'm not nervous at all.

52:09.125 --> 52:10.460
What?

52:15.882 --> 52:17.133
A message!

52:18.468 --> 52:19.886
- A message came?
- Yes!

52:20.679 --> 52:22.013
They'll buy it right away!

52:22.681 --> 52:24.015
That's great.

52:28.144 --> 52:29.771
Thank you. I'll use it well.

52:30.272 --> 52:31.439
Thank you.

52:46.413 --> 52:47.789
Thanks for everything.

52:48.456 --> 52:50.292
Buy me dinner then.

52:52.043 --> 52:54.462
- What do you mean?
- I mean I'm hungry.

52:55.046 --> 52:56.214
Does it have to mean something else?

52:57.966 --> 52:58.884
No.

52:59.467 --> 53:01.094
What do you want to eat, Forecaster Lee?

53:02.554 --> 53:03.889
Anything.

53:04.973 --> 53:06.016
Let's go.

53:16.318 --> 53:23.199
Pale pink skirt

53:24.034 --> 53:30.332
Fluttered in the spring wind

53:31.124 --> 53:37.589
While chewing on my coat string as usual

53:38.256 --> 53:44.804
On the way to the village shrine
Where wild orchids bloom

53:44.888 --> 53:48.892
When flowers bloomed

54:36.189 --> 54:37.941
The time between seasons is ambiguous.

54:38.483 --> 54:41.987
It's hard to say if it's cold or hot.

54:42.654 --> 54:46.741
But as the hot summer
eventually comes after spring passes,

54:47.450 --> 54:49.744
once this ambiguous period is over,

54:50.495 --> 54:54.124
flowers of another season bloom
before I even know it.

54:56.459 --> 54:58.294
Here's the food you ordered.

55:07.887 --> 55:09.305
You're selling that apartment?

55:10.515 --> 55:11.558
Yes.

55:11.641 --> 55:13.852
- It's too bad.
- It is.

55:14.394 --> 55:15.770
I'd live there if I were you.

55:16.396 --> 55:18.189
You don't know, but that apartment--

55:18.273 --> 55:19.566
I know a little.

55:20.316 --> 55:22.068
Oh, right.

55:23.737 --> 55:26.031
There are too many things
that remind me of him.

55:26.614 --> 55:28.283
The only solution is to dispose of them.

55:28.366 --> 55:29.993
How can you do that?

55:30.785 --> 55:32.078
What about your heart then?

55:32.162 --> 55:34.497
Can you dispose of your heart

55:34.581 --> 55:36.374
just because it no longer loves him?

55:37.500 --> 55:39.753
I should still get rid
of everything that reminds me.

55:40.628 --> 55:42.464
Even so, you'll regret it anyway.

55:44.424 --> 55:46.634
You can't undo something that's been done.

55:46.718 --> 55:49.512
You probably mean nothing to him now.

55:50.263 --> 55:51.931
So maybe you're making a loss.

55:52.015 --> 55:53.808
Honestly, it's a pity.

55:59.147 --> 56:01.316
I don't want you to go through that.

56:05.695 --> 56:06.863
Are you worried about me?

56:07.614 --> 56:10.325
It's my advice from experience.

56:10.909 --> 56:12.452
No, thanks.

56:16.664 --> 56:17.791
Did you take the medicine?

56:18.458 --> 56:19.793
Just eat the chicken.

56:32.430 --> 56:33.515
What are you doing?

56:34.557 --> 56:37.018
I see you took them.

56:39.896 --> 56:41.397
Your fever broke.

56:48.363 --> 56:52.117
As expected, the time
between seasons is ambiguous.

56:55.537 --> 56:57.872
- This place is nice.
- Welcome.

56:57.956 --> 56:59.457
- How many?
- Three.

56:59.541 --> 57:01.334
- Three? Please wait.
- What's wrong?

57:01.918 --> 57:03.545
Look over there.

57:04.337 --> 57:06.131
- That table is empty.
- What?

57:06.214 --> 57:08.591
- Let me clear the table first.
- Hey.

57:08.675 --> 57:09.801
But why are you hiding?

57:11.553 --> 57:12.804
But why are you hiding?

57:12.887 --> 57:14.472
Because they can't find out.

57:14.556 --> 57:15.932
Find out what?

57:16.766 --> 57:19.185
About you and me. Don't you understand?

57:21.479 --> 57:23.189
They're coming this way.

57:25.525 --> 57:27.026
Hey, where are you going?

57:27.110 --> 57:28.153
He…

57:28.987 --> 57:30.488
He must be insane.

57:31.030 --> 57:32.240
Please wait.

57:34.033 --> 57:35.535
- What?
- What?

57:36.035 --> 57:36.953
What are you doing here?

57:37.036 --> 57:39.581
Assistant Director Shin said
this place has great fried chicken.

57:39.664 --> 57:40.957
What about you?

57:41.040 --> 57:43.585
Someone I know said
the chicken here was good.

57:43.668 --> 57:44.794
We came here to drink.

57:47.505 --> 57:48.840
Someone you know?

57:50.884 --> 57:51.801
Hey!

58:02.353 --> 58:03.897
That's not him.

58:03.980 --> 58:05.565
I thought it was someone I knew.

58:13.615 --> 58:14.824
You're silly.

58:16.743 --> 58:19.120
Do you want to have a drink with us?

58:19.204 --> 58:21.623
No, something urgent came up,
so I have to go.

58:22.207 --> 58:23.833
- You guys enjoy.
- Okay.

58:23.917 --> 58:25.293
- Bye.
- Bye.

58:25.376 --> 58:26.794
Bye.

58:28.713 --> 58:30.507
- Please come this way.
- Okay.

58:50.235 --> 58:51.069
Come here.

59:01.538 --> 59:02.580
What happened?

59:02.664 --> 59:04.749
Did they notice? They didn't, right?

59:06.376 --> 59:07.710
Did they?

59:07.794 --> 59:09.295
What are you doing?

59:10.171 --> 59:11.381
What do you mean?

59:11.464 --> 59:12.549
Do we have something

59:13.049 --> 59:14.801
to hide from the others?

59:16.219 --> 59:18.888
If we drink at a place like this together,

59:18.972 --> 59:21.099
they'll misunderstand us.

59:21.182 --> 59:25.186
We can't have rumors
going around about us.

59:29.315 --> 59:30.942
That's a bit too close.

59:35.405 --> 59:36.698
Do you have feelings for me?

59:42.120 --> 59:43.204
No. Why?

59:43.288 --> 59:44.747
I think you do.

59:46.541 --> 59:47.458
No, I don't.

59:58.511 --> 01:00:00.096
Does it seem like I do?

01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:04.976
Just so you know, I don't flirt around.

01:00:06.227 --> 01:00:08.354
Hey, I didn't ask you to flirt with me.

01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:12.442
- Then do you want to go out with me?
- What? You said you wouldn't ask me out.

01:00:12.525 --> 01:00:16.279
That's because I can't ask you out
if I'm the only one who has feelings.

01:00:22.869 --> 01:00:24.245
If we like each other, we can go out.

01:00:24.329 --> 01:00:27.206
If not, we won't.

01:00:31.169 --> 01:00:32.587
So what are we?

01:00:35.048 --> 01:00:38.051
What are we to you?

01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:23.638
The recent collision happened

01:01:23.721 --> 01:01:27.100
because the drivers' visibility
dropped due to the fog.

01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.852
Why doesn't our country
give fog advisories?

01:01:30.478 --> 01:01:33.106
A reporter shouldn't distort the facts.

01:01:33.189 --> 01:01:35.191
You should've done your research
before going up against her.

01:01:35.274 --> 01:01:39.487
Ha-kyung beat all the competition
and became the youngest director.

01:01:39.570 --> 01:01:40.780
- What about the rest?
- And the details?

01:01:40.863 --> 01:01:42.323
I think she works here.

01:01:42.407 --> 01:01:43.783
It's obvious he's dating a colleague.

01:01:43.866 --> 01:01:45.034
Thank you. You can go now.

01:01:45.535 --> 01:01:48.037
What was that? Was she hazing him?

01:01:48.121 --> 01:01:49.038
How do I turn this off?

01:01:49.122 --> 01:01:49.997
Hello, Forecaster Lee.

01:01:50.081 --> 01:01:51.874
I want you to find cases
from countries around the world

01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:54.043
that frequently have fogs like we do
and put them on my desk.

01:01:54.127 --> 01:01:55.253
What's all this?

01:01:55.336 --> 01:01:56.295
Did I waste my time?

01:01:57.338 --> 01:01:59.132
Office romance will be the death of me.

01:01:59.215 --> 01:02:03.928
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
